{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/543097-liber-monstrorum-aka-let-s-give-mythological-monsters-a-beast-write-up","id":543097,"title":"Liber Monstrorum (aka \"let's give mythological monsters a Beast write-up)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-06T15:28:30-07:00","id":543097,"title":"Liber Monstrorum (aka \"let's give mythological monsters a Beast write-up)","content":"Now that we have access to to preliminary text of Beast, we can do something I've been thinking about since the game's announcement: a thread where we take a monster from the myths and translate it into Beast terms. I've always been fascinated by all kind of mythologies and thus I'm having way too much fun at this but, my personal entertainment aside, this discussion might actually prove pretty useful to inspire others and give examples of Beast's versatility. <br /> <br /> Let's turn it in a game: I write the first monster and ask for a specific other. Whoever writes it up suggests the following one and so on.<br /> <br /> For starters, one of my favorites:<br /> <br /> <b>The Chimera </b>(from Greek myths)<br /> <br /> Eshmaki Ravager, slayed by Bellerophon<br /> <br /> Atavism: Basilisk's Touch, Dragonfire, Limb from Limb, <br /> <br /> Nightmares: All Your Teeth Are Falling Out, Flying and Falling<br /> <br /> Lair: a volcanic area surrouded by woods where geothermical activities spread all kind of noxious gases around and feed the numerous flames which erupt from the ground. A few lakes are scattered around the lair but the water is poisonous as well. <i>Extreme Heat, Fog, Stench, Stinging, Exposed, Noxious Gasses, Toxic (water)</i><br /> <br /> <br /> And there's that. For the next one, I'd like to see Charybdis, from the Odyssey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"htt